.TH DDPAR 1 "2026-10-17" "ddpar 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ddpar \- clone or back up files and block devices in parallel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ddpar
.BI \-i " input"
.BI \-o " output"
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Split an input file or block device into segments and process them with
parallel GNU dd workers. The last segment includes any remaining bytes.
The commands are also available with a .sh suffix.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i " path" ", \-\-input " path
Source file or block device. Always local.
.TP
.BI \-o " path" ", \-\-output " path
Clone destination (file, directory or block device), or backup directory.
With remote operation, this path belongs to the remote host.
.TP
.BI \-m " clone|backup"
Operation mode (default: clone).
.TP
.BI \-j " number"
Number of parallel workers, a positive decimal integer (default: 4).
.TP
.BI \-b " bytes"
Block size, a positive decimal integer (default: 1048576).
.TP
.BI \-n " name"
Backup basename, without a directory component. Backup mode only.
The default is the input basename.
.TP
.B \-c
Request gzip compression at level 6.
Local compression is supported for backups. Clone compression requires
remote mode c; otherwise the clone proceeds uncompressed with a warning.
.TP
.B \-s
Create SHA256 files for local backup parts. Not applied to remote backups.
.TP
.B \-f
Force an operation despite overwrite protection. Use with care.
.TP
.BR \-r " [n|c]"
Enable remote operation. Mode n is the default and compresses locally;
mode c uses gzip on the remote side. Mode l is unsupported and rejected.
.TP
.BI \-R " [user@]host"
SSH host or SSH configuration alias. Also enables remote operation.
.TP
.B \-d
Enable shell tracing. Debug output can expose passwords.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show built-in help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COMPRESSION
Set to 1 to request compression, or 0 to disable it (default: 0).
.TP
.B COMPRESSION_LEVEL
Gzip level from 1 through 9 when enabled through COMPRESSION (default: 6).
The command-line flag \-c resets this level to 6.
.TP
.B CHECKSUM
Set to 1 to request local backup checksums, or 0 to disable them (default: 0).
The command-line flags \-c and \-s enable their respective features.
.TP
.B DDPAR_NETWORK_TIMEOUT
Netcat inactivity timeout in seconds (default: 300).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ddpar \-i /dev/sdb \-o /mnt/backups \-m backup \-c \-s
ddpar \-i source.img \-o clone.img \-j 8
ddpar \-i /dev/sdb \-o /backup \-m backup \-r n \-R user@host
.fi
.SH NOTES
Do not modify the source during a transfer. Files and block devices may
be overwritten. Remote payloads use unencrypted netcat; only the SSH
control channel is encrypted. Use remote transfers on trusted networks.
The remote host needs the commands described in the installed README.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates an error or a refused operation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dd (1),
.BR ddpar-restore (1),
.BR ddpar-check (1)
